From 2dc6e367acded8e79282d80c1975ebffc23d2144 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 07:15:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] H2 remainder: card_change_pass idle skip +
 hot-forever probe inputs (C11)

Why (H2 run 132120, P1 on hub PID 2145361): host_pass 2.855% of a core vs <=0.5%. Every
sub-pass recorded 0 skips in 19 runs: card_change_pass fallbacks=19, notices/guarantee/killed
fallbacks=19 (probe pending every pass), delegation changes=19 (key moved every pass).

Five whys, from hub state.db read-only:
- guarantee_pass: one 3-day-old kanban_notice with no closeout is returned by the probe, but
  candidates() never offers a non-deferred row past LOOKBACK_S, so the pass was hot forever.
  The key also carried the whole state.db revision, which any chat write moves.
- killed_notices: 73 children reaped long ago keep the probe positive, but the consumer only
  re-offers children reaped inside RETRY_WINDOW_S (24 h).
- notices: subs whose chat is live are skipped by the sweep, yet counted as pending; the live
  set is already in the key, so the chat unloading moves it.
- delegation/killed/notices/guarantee keys carried a store/board revision that bookkeeping and
  chat writes move constantly, although each probe re-proves its own emptiness.
- card_change_pass opened a board connection (schema prepare: 121 of 647 samples) every pass
  and refreshed a chat's outcome once per changed card (outcome refresh: 439 samples).

Change:
- card_change_pass: the durable task_events cursor against the board's retained reader is the
  skip key (_board_idle); no connect when equal. Changed boards fan out per chat: marks per
  card, ONE outcome refresh per chat per pass.
- guarantee probe mirrors the lookback and keys on the candidate rows, not the store revision;
  killed probe applies the retry window; notices probe takes the live set; delegation/killed/
  notices keys drop the store revision (quiet/empty is re-proved on every probe).
- Pending busy-chat / wake-slot deferrals, in-flight claims and unknown inputs still disable
  every skip; due times unchanged.

Proof: tests/tui_gateway/test_h2_remainder_c11.py (13 tests; 9 RED on origin/main, GREEN here),
incl. outcome change within one pass, unchanged inputs skipped without a connect, deferral
retried after its due time, chat unloading with a pending notice, and a 200-pass replay
benchmark (idle pass 2.7 ms vs 9.5 ms connect-per-pass, ratio 0.28). 317 tests across the 16
unloaded/fanout/outcome files pass; scripts/check health ok. Remote half of card_change_pass
(H3's remote index) is untouched and still always runs.
